  ## 4. File-IO (FieldTrip) and BioSig

  ### 4.1 pop_fileio [V]
  `pop_fileio.m` is **core** (`functions/popfunc/`, BSD-2), not part of the plugin. Header: "POP_FILEIO - import data files into EEGLAB using FileIO ... >> OUTEEG = pop_fileio( filename ); >> OUTEEG = pop_fileio( header, dat, evt ); 'dataformat' - [string] data format. Default is automatic. Available choices are available in ft_read_data ... Note: FILEIO toolbox must be installed." Flow: `if ~plugin_askinstall('Fileio', 'ft_read_data'), return; end` (64) -> `dat = ft_read_header(filename);` (105 GUI / 152 scripted; **no headerformat option, so header detection is purely ft_filetype**) -> `'dataformat'` forwarded only if not 'auto' (199) -> `ft_read_data(filename,'header',dat,dataopts{:})` (203) -> `ft_read_event(filename, dataopts{:})` (382). GUI lists ~100 hard-coded format names (91-100). Fills `EEG.srate = dat.Fs; EEG.nbchan = dat.nChans; EEG.data = alldata; EEG.setname=''; EEG.comments=['Original file: ' filename]; EEG.xmin = -dat.nSamplesPre/EEG.srate; EEG.trials = dat.nTrials;` (240-246), chanlocs labels/type/XYZ from dat.label/chantype/elec (258-345), `EEG.etc.fileio_dat = dat` (343).

  ### 4.2 The Fileio plugin [V/I]
  It is a dated snapshot of FieldTrip's fileio module: `eeglab.prj` lists `plugins/Fileio250523` and `plugins/Fieldtrip-lite250523` (+ `.../external/biosig`) (lines 123-130) = 2025-05-23 snapshots [V]. eeglab.m special-cases folders containing `fieldtrip` (adds compat/forward/utilities/plotting, removes external/*) and sets version 'ersion unknowned' for fieldtrip/fileio folders (1059-1091, 1116-1121) [V]. Wiki: "FileIO (https://github.com/fieldtrip/fileio): Toolbox allowing data import in multiple data formats" (EEGLAB_Extensions.md:136). fieldtrip/fileio repo = exactly the module (ft_read_header/data/event, ft_filetype, private/, GPL-3 COPYING); its log is "synchronized with main FieldTrip repository" commits (last ten 2026-06-24..2026-09-24) [V+W]. Repackaging is undocumented; naming `Fileio<yymmdd>` and the compile recipe ("Do not use the GIT version of FieldTrip ... Instead get the latest plugin", Compiled_EEGLAB.md:210-219) indicate SCCN uploads a snapshot around each ~annual release [I]. **Lag from FieldTrip merge to manager users: months to ~1 year**, unless users install FieldTrip itself [I].

  ### 4.3 Would a FieldTrip-side Cadwell reader auto-appear? [V]
  Only if `ft_filetype` recognises the file (pop_fileio passes no `headerformat`). `ft_read_header.m:17` "'headerformat' = name of a MATLAB function that takes the filename as input (default is automatic)"; line 44 "To use an external reading function, you can specify an external function as the 'headerformat' option ... search for BIDS_TSV as example"; ft_read_data (34) / ft_read_event accept function names for dataformat/eventformat. mffmatlabio uses exactly this hook (`mff_fileio_read_header.m` etc.) [V]. But pop_fileio only forwards `'dataformat'`, never headerformat, so the GUI needs ft_filetype support. `ft_filetype.m` (master 2026-09-28) has **no** cadwell/ezdata/sqlite detection (only `.easy` -> `neuroelectrics_easy`, 1290) [V]. So: a FieldTrip PR touching ft_filetype.m, ft_read_header/data/event.m + `private/read_cadwell_*.m`; a SQLite dependency (`sqlite()` = Database Toolbox R2022a+, or mksqlite MEX) would be a first for fileio [I]. ft_read_header also has `'fallback' = 'biosig'` (12) [V].

  ### 4.4 BioSig and Cadwell [V]
  pop_biosig -> sopen/sread from the Biosig plugin (eeglab.m:1095-1099 adds `<Biosig>/biosig/t200_FileAccess`). MATLAB `sopen.m` (two GitHub mirrors, 494-506 kB) has **no** cadwell/ezdata/EASY string [V; older mirrors, current GitLab blocked]. biosig4c++ has `t210/sopen_cadwell_read.c` (Copyright 2021 Alois Schloegl, GPL-3), comment "read CADWELL file formats (EAS, EZ3, ARC)"; all three branches end in `biosigERROR(hdr, B4C_FORMAT_UNSUPPORTED, "Format EAS(Cadwell): unsupported ")` / EZ3 / ARC (lines 92, 287, 291) - a reverse-engineering stub, plus sibling `sopen_sqlite.c` [V]. SourceForge feature request #13 "Support for AES, EZ3, and ARC fiile formats" (2021-08-27, open; comment 2021-09-30: "sopen_cadwell.c and sopen_sqlite.c are used to develop tools for reverse engineering") [W]. Nothing about `.ezdata`. BioSig cannot read Cadwell today.

